('2d64b518-80a3-58a9-8dba-566cabee277d', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '8e9dd5f1-dd78-4ce4-8525-76c12991e03f', 'a-level', '28.7', '9702 coursebook 28.7 · Explaining the origin of line spectra', 43, 43, 'Hydrogen atoms are excited to the n = 3 level (−1.51 eV); the lower levels are −3.40 eV and −13.6 eV. (a) List the possible transitions back to the ground state. (b) Calculate each photon energy. (c) Calculate the shortest wavelength emitted, in nm. Give only the answer to (c). Take h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s, c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹ and e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '102.8 nm', 'nm', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 3 → 1, 3 → 2, 2 → 1. (b) 12.09 eV, 1.89 eV and 10.2 eV. (c) Largest energy 12.09 eV: λ = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ × 3.00 × 10⁸ ÷ (12.09 × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 1.028 × 10⁻⁷ m. In nm: 1.028 × 10⁻⁷ × 10⁹ = 103. Mark scheme (6 marks). B1: three transitions. C1: photon energies. M1: largest energy gives shortest λ. C1: J conversion. C1: value. A1: λ = 103 nm.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 280" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg78d15414-t fg78d15414-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg78d15414-t">Hydrogen energy levels</title><desc id="fg78d15414-d">Energy level diagram for hydrogen showing the n = 3 level at −1.51 eV, n = 2 at −3.40 eV and the ground state at −13.6 eV.</desc><line x1="110" y1="258" x2="290" y2="258" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="102" y="258" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">n = 1</text><text x="298" y="258" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">−13.6 eV</text><line x1="110" y1="77.5" x2="290" y2="77.5" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="102" y="77.5" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">n = 2</text><text x="298" y="77.5" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">−3.40 eV</text><line x1="110" y1="44" x2="290" y2="44" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="102" y="44" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">n = 3</text><text x="298" y="44" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">−1.51 eV</text><text x="14" y="12" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">energy / eV</text><line x1="14" y1="266" x2="14" y2="24" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="14,20 17,26.3 11,26.3" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/></svg>', 'Energy level diagram for hydrogen showing the n = 3 level at −1.51 eV, n = 2 at −3.40 eV and the ground state at −13.6 eV.'),
('4c264b0d-e435-5e5c-960c-e8899891de49', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '8e9dd5f1-dd78-4ce4-8525-76c12991e03f', 'a-level', '28.7', '9702 coursebook 28.7 · Explaining the origin of line spectra', 44, 44, 'Electrons with 12.2 eV of kinetic energy pass through hydrogen gas in the ground state (levels −13.6, −3.40, −1.51, −0.85 eV). (a) State the highest level that can be reached. (b) List the lines that can then be emitted. (c) Calculate the longest wavelength emitted, in nm. Give only the answer to (c). Take h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s, c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹ and e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '657.7 nm', 'nm', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) −1.51 eV (needs 12.09 eV); −0.85 eV needs 12.75 eV. (b) 3 → 2, 3 → 1 and 2 → 1. (c) Smallest gap = 3.40 − 1.51 = 1.89 eV: λ = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ × 3.00 × 10⁸ ÷ (1.89 × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 6.577 × 10⁻⁷ m. In nm: 6.577 × 10⁻⁷ × 10⁹ = 658. Mark scheme (5 marks). B1: n = 3 reached. B1: three lines. M1: smallest gap. C1: value. A1: λ = 658 nm.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 288.9" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgbb5a1fa0-t fgbb5a1fa0-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgbb5a1fa0-t">Hydrogen energy levels</title><desc id="fgbb5a1fa0-d">Energy level diagram for hydrogen with levels at −13.6 eV, −3.40 eV, −1.51 eV and −0.85 eV.</desc><line x1="110" y1="266.9" x2="290" y2="266.9" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="102" y="266.9" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">n = 1</text><text x="298" y="266.9" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">−13.6 eV</text><line x1="110" y1="95.7" x2="290" y2="95.7" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="102" y="95.7" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">n = 2</text><text x="298" y="95.7" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">−3.40 eV</text><line x1="110" y1="64" x2="290" y2="64" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="102" y="64" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">n = 3</text><text x="298" y="64" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">−1.51 eV</text><line x1="110" y1="44" x2="290" y2="44" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="102" y="44" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">n = 4</text><text x="298" y="44" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">−0.85 eV</text><text x="14" y="12" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">energy / eV</text><line x1="14" y1="274.9" x2="14" y2="24" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="14,20 17,26.3 11,26.3" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/></svg>', 'Energy level diagram for hydrogen with levels at −13.6 eV, −3.40 eV, −1.51 eV and −0.85 eV.'),
('2c077de7-2296-5587-8fa8-0241415c41bd', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '8e9dd5f1-dd78-4ce4-8525-76c12991e03f', 'a-level', '28.7', '9702 coursebook 28.7 · Explaining the origin of line spectra', 45, 45, 'Sodium vapour absorbs 2.0 mW from a beam of 589 nm light. (a) Calculate the photon energy. (b) Calculate the number of photons absorbed per second. (c) Explain why the vapour does not heat up steadily as a result. Give only the answer to (b). Take h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s and c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '5.923e15', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) E = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ × 3.00 × 10⁸ ÷ 589 × 10⁻⁹ = 3.377 × 10⁻¹⁹ J. (b) n = 2.0 × 10⁻³ ÷ 3.377 × 10⁻¹⁹ = 5.92 × 10¹⁵. (c) The excited atoms re-emit photons of the same energy, in all directions. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: photon energy. M1: n = P/E. C1: mW to W. C1: value. B1: re-emission in all directions. A1: n = 5.92 × 10¹⁵.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('66ed0aea-2d7d-5338-950e-55509bd82f9c', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '8e9dd5f1-dd78-4ce4-8525-76c12991e03f', 'a-level', '28.7', '9702 coursebook 28.7 · Explaining the origin of line spectra', 46, 46, 'The 656 nm hydrogen line is seen in the first order at 23.2° with an unlabelled grating. (a) Calculate the slit spacing. (b) Calculate the number of lines per mm on the grating.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '600.5', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) d = λ/sin θ = 656 × 10⁻⁹ ÷ sin 23.2° = 1.665 × 10⁻⁶ m. (b) Lines per mm = 1 ÷ (1.665 × 10⁻⁶ × 10³) = 601. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: d = λ/sin θ. C1: value. M1: lines per mm = 1/d with d in mm. C1: value. A1: N = 601.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 280" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg4af00526-t fg4af00526-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg4af00526-t">Measuring a grating</title><desc id="fg4af00526-d">The 656 nm hydrogen line leaves the grating in the first order at 23.2° to the straight-through beam.</desc><line x1="20" y1="140" x2="140" y2="140" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="110,140 102.7,143.4 102.7,136.6" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><line x1="140" y1="30" x2="140" y2="250" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="36" x2="144" y2="36" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="44" x2="144" y2="44" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="52" x2="144" y2="52" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="60" x2="144" y2="60" style="stroke:c