<line x1="140" y1="140" x2="335.2" y2="223.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="340.4,225.9 332.4,226.1 335,219.9" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><path d="M210,140 A70,70 0 0,0 204.3,112.4" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="224.2" y="122.7" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">23.2°</text><text x="140" y="18" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">grating</text></svg>', 'The 656 nm hydrogen line leaves the grating in the first order at 23.2° to the straight-through beam.'),
('d11e2f44-a20e-5132-a1af-ab64068d022f', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '8e9dd5f1-dd78-4ce4-8525-76c12991e03f', 'a-level', '28.7', '9702 coursebook 28.7 · Explaining the origin of line spectra', 47, 47, 'An atom with three energy levels emits lines with photon energies of 1.5 eV, 2.5 eV and 4.0 eV. Its ground state is at −6.0 eV. (a) Explain why 1.5 + 2.5 = 4.0. (b) Find the energies of the other two levels. (c) Calculate the wavelength of the 1.5 eV line, in nm. Give only the answer to (c). Take h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s, c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹ and e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '828.8 nm', 'nm', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) The 4.0 eV line is the direct drop from top to ground; the other two are the same drop in two steps. (b) −6.0 + 2.5 = −3.5 eV and −6.0 + 4.0 = −2.0 eV. (c) λ = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ × 3.00 × 10⁸ ÷ (1.5 × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 8.288 × 10⁻⁷ m. In nm: 8.288 × 10⁻⁷ × 10⁹ = 829. Mark scheme (6 marks). B1: energy conservation. C1: middle level. C1: top level. M1: λ = hc/E. C1: value. A1: λ = 829 nm.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 250" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg6d07d9cd-t fg6d07d9cd-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg6d07d9cd-t">Three-level atom</title><desc id="fg6d07d9cd-d">Energy level diagram of an atom with its ground state at −6.0 eV and two higher levels, with the three possible downward transitions marked.</desc><line x1="110" y1="228" x2="290" y2="228" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="102" y="228" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">ground state</text><text x="298" y="228" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">−6.0 eV</text><line x1="110" y1="113" x2="290" y2="113" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="110" y1="44" x2="290" y2="44" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="155" y1="44" x2="155" y2="106.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="155,113 151.2,104.8 158.8,104.8" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="200" y1="113" x2="200" y2="221.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="200,228 196.2,219.8 203.8,219.8" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="245" y1="44" x2="245" y2="221.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="245,228 241.2,219.8 248.8,219.8" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><text x="14" y="12" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">energy / eV</text><line x1="14" y1="236" x2="14" y2="24" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="14,20 17,26.3 11,26.3" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/></svg>', 'Energy level diagram of an atom with its ground state at −6.0 eV and two higher levels, with the three possible downward transitions marked.'),
('a7738b29-8697-5579-8739-ab6a5fa59f3a', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '8e9dd5f1-dd78-4ce4-8525-76c12991e03f', 'a-level', '28.7', '9702 coursebook 28.7 · Explaining the origin of line spectra', 48, 48, 'Light from a hydrogen lamp falls on a grating with 300 lines per mm. (a) Calculate the slit spacing. (b) Calculate the angle of the 656 nm line in the third order, in degrees. (c) State whether a fourth order exists for this line.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '36.19', '°', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) d = 1 ÷ 300 × 10³ = 3.333 × 10⁻⁶ m. (b) sin θ = 3 × 656 × 10⁻⁹ ÷ 3.333 × 10⁻⁶ = 0.5904, θ = sin⁻¹ 0.5904 = 36.2°. (c) For n = 5, sin θ > 1, but n = 4 gives 0.787, so a fourth order exists. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: d. M1: nλ = d sin θ. C1: value. B1: fourth order check. A1: θ = 36.2°.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 280" role="img" aria-labelledby="fge609005f-t fge609005f-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fge609005f-t">Orders from a grating</title><desc id="fge609005f-d">The 656 nm hydrogen line falls on a grating with 300 lines per mm; the first three orders leave at increasing angles on each side.</desc><line x1="20" y1="140" x2="140" y2="140" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="110,140 102.7,143.4 102.7,136.6" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><line x1="140" y1="30" x2="140" y2="250" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="36" x2="144" y2="36" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="44" x2="144" y2="44" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="52" x2="144" y2="52" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="60" x2="144" y2="60" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="68" x2="144" y2="68" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="76" x2="144" y2="76" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="84" x2="144" y2="84" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="92" x2="144" y2="92" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="100" x2="144" y2="100" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="108" x2="144" y2="108" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="116" x2="144" y2="116" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="124" x2="144" y2="124" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="132" x2="144" y2="132" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="140" x2="144" y2="140" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="148" x2="144" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="156" x2="144" y2="156" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="164" x2="144" y2="164" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="172" x2="144" y2="172" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="180" x2="144" y2="180" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="188" x2="144" y2="188" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="196" x2="144" y2="196" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="204" x2="144" y2="204" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="212" x2="144" y2="212" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="220" x2="144" y2="220" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="228" x2="144" y2="228" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="236" x2="144" y2="236" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136" y1="244" x2="144" y2="244" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="140" y1="140" x2="358" y2="140" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:4 3"/><text x="362" y="140" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">n = 0</text><line x1="140" y1="140" x2="348.2" y2="98.2" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="353.7,97.1 347.3,101.8 346,95.2" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><text x="357.7" y="93.1" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">n = 1</text><line x1="140" y1="140" x2="335.3" y2="56.4" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="340.4,54.2 335.1,60.2 332.4,53.9" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><text x="344.4" y="50.2" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">n = 2</text><line x1="140" y1="140" x2="285.9" y2="33.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="290.4,30 286.5,37 282.5,31.6" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><text x="294.4" y="26" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">n = 3</text><text x="140" y="18" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">grating</text><text x="140" y="266" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">300 lines per mm</text></svg>', 'The 656 nm hydrogen line falls on a grating with 300 lines per mm; the first three orders leave at increasing angles on each side.'),
('4b1ef190-6574-53cd-bb23-ade9f961d664', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '8e9dd5f1-dd78-4ce4-8525-76c12991e03f', 'a-level', '28.7', '9702 coursebook 28.7 · Explaining the origin of line spectra', 49, 49, 'A 10 W fluorescent tube converts 60% of its input power into ultraviolet photons of wavelength 254 nm from mercury atoms. (a) Calculate the ultraviolet power. (b) Calculate the photon energy. (c) Calculate the number of ultraviolet photons emitted per second. Give only the answer to (c). Take h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s and c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '7.662e18', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 0.60 × 10 = 6.0 W. (b) E = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ × 3.00 × 10⁸ ÷ 254 × 10⁻⁹ = 7.831 × 10⁻¹⁹ J. (c) n = 6.0 ÷ 7.831 × 10⁻¹⁹ = 7.66 × 10¹⁸. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: UV power. C1: photon energy. M1: n = P/E. C1: value. B1: units consistent. A1: n = 7.66 × 10¹⁸.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('d613a15e-3eed-55a0-8779-7c5200519ee5', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '8e9dd5f1-dd78-4ce4-8525-76c12991e03f', 'a-level', '28.7', '9702 coursebook 28.7 · Explaining the origin of line spectra', 50, 50, 'Electrons accelerated through 10.0 V pass through mercury vapour, whose first excitation energy is 4.9 eV. (a) Explain why an electron can excite at most two atoms. (b) Calculate the wavelength of the light emitted when an excited atom returns to its ground state, in nm. Give only the answer to (b). Take h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s, c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹ and e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '253.7 nm', 'nm', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 10.0 eV ÷ 4.9 eV ≈ 2.04, so two excitations use 9.8 eV and 0.2 eV is left. (b) λ = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ × 3.00 × 10⁸ ÷ (4.9 × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 2.537 × 10⁻⁷ m. In nm: 2.537 × 10⁻⁷ × 10⁹ = 254. Mark scheme (5 marks). B1: 10.0 eV gives two lots of 4.9 eV. M1: λ = hc/E. C1: conversion. C1: value. A1: λ = 254 nm.', 5, NULL, NULL)
