y1="125" x2="382" y2="116" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:3 3"/><text x="160" y="86" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0.50 mm</text><line x1="158" y1="92" x2="152" y2="107" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="150,220 156.3,217 156.3,223" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><line x1="154.9" y1="220" x2="377.1" y2="220" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="382,220 375.7,223 375.7,217" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><text x="266" y="232" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1.5 m</text><polygon points="372,160 375,166.3 369,166.3" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><line x1="372" y1="164.9" x2="372" y2="177.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="372,182 369,175.7 375,175.7" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><text x="366" y="171" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">x</text><text x="150" y="22" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">double slit</text><text x="382" y="18" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">screen</text></svg>', 'Laser light of wavelength 600 nm passes through two slits 0.50 mm apart; bright fringes form on a screen 1.5 m away.'),
('64455f1b-688e-5d77-8315-034a656d8a61', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '7ea4a576-84c8-4a0f-9474-20a442190683', 'a-level', '28.9', '9702 coursebook 28.9 · The nature of light: waves or particles?', 10, 10, 'Who first explained the photoelectric effect by treating light as made of quanta?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Albert Einstein', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Einstein proposed light quanta (photons) in 1905. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: D (Albert Einstein).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('cd96168c-6a57-537b-ab6e-a6a14ef58d09', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '7ea4a576-84c8-4a0f-9474-20a442190683', 'a-level', '28.9', '9702 coursebook 28.9 · The nature of light: waves or particles?', 11, 11, 'A blue photon has a wavelength of 470 nm. Calculate its energy in units of 10⁻¹⁹ J. Take h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s and c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '4.232', '10⁻¹⁹ J', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'E = hc/λ = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ × 3.00 × 10⁸ ÷ 470 × 10⁻⁹ = 4.23 × 10⁻¹⁹ J. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: E = hc/λ. A1: E = 4.23 × 10⁻¹⁹ J.', 2, NULL, NULL),
('7cdd306e-bc52-5762-8229-61d539c5e55d', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '7ea4a576-84c8-4a0f-9474-20a442190683', 'a-level', '28.9', '9702 coursebook 28.9 · The nature of light: waves or particles?', 12, 12, 'What does the polarisation of light show?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Light is a transverse wave', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Only transverse waves can be polarised. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: B (Light is a transverse wave).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('7d02de67-74b8-5b4e-8357-c80b6bdb87d8', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '7ea4a576-84c8-4a0f-9474-20a442190683', 'a-level', '28.9', '9702 coursebook 28.9 · The nature of light: waves or particles?', 13, 13, 'A detector counts 3.0 × 10⁴ photons per second, each of energy 3.3 × 10⁻¹⁹ J. Calculate the power it receives, in units of 10⁻¹⁴ W.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.99', '10⁻¹⁴ W', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'P = nE = 3.0 × 10⁴ × 3.3 × 10⁻¹⁹ = 9.90 × 10⁻¹⁵ J s⁻¹. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: P = nE. A1: P = 0.99 × 10⁻¹⁴ W.', 2, NULL, NULL),
('0e957e3d-be84-5a79-a89b-484fcdb8f1c7', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '7ea4a576-84c8-4a0f-9474-20a442190683', 'a-level', '28.9', '9702 coursebook 28.9 · The nature of light: waves or particles?', 14, 14, 'When a two-slit pattern is built up from very dim light, how does each photon arrive at the screen?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'As a single localised spot', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Individual detections are particle-like; the pattern emerges from many of them. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: C (As a single localised spot).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('0ba22212-4150-5e05-8822-5e247abbbb52', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '7ea4a576-84c8-4a0f-9474-20a442190683', 'a-level', '28.9', '9702 coursebook 28.9 · The nature of light: waves or particles?', 15, 15, 'Two slits 0.50 mm apart give fringes 2.4 mm apart on a screen 2.0 m away. Calculate the wavelength in nm.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '600 nm', 'nm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'λ = ax/D = 0.50 × 10⁻³ × 2.4 × 10⁻³ ÷ 2.0 = 6.000 × 10⁻⁷ m. In nm: 6.000 × 10⁻⁷ × 10⁹ = 600. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: λ = ax/D. A1: λ = 600 nm.', 2, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 440 250" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg4bcf446f-t fg4bcf446f-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg4bcf446f-t">Two-slit fringes</title><desc id="fg4bcf446f-d">Two slits 0.50 mm apart produce bright fringes 2.4 mm apart on a screen 2.0 m away.</desc><rect x="18" y="104" width="56" height="24" rx="3" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="46" y="142" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">laser</text><line x1="74" y1="116" x2="150" y2="116" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="150" y1="34" x2="150" y2="103" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="150" y1="111" x2="150" y2="121" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="150" y1="129" x2="150" y2="200" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="30" x2="382" y2="204" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="385" y="24.1" width="14" height="7.8" rx="0" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="385" y="45.7" width="14" height="8.6" rx="0" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="385" y="67.3" width="14" height="9.4" rx="0" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="385" y="88.9" width="14" height="10.2" rx="0" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="385" y="110.5" width="14" height="11" rx="0" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="385" y="132.9" width="14" height="10.2" rx="0" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="385" y="155.3" width="14" height="9.4" rx="0" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="385" y="177.7" width="14" height="8.6" rx="0" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="385" y="200.1" width="14" height="7.8" rx="0" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="150" y1="107" x2="382" y2="116" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:3 3"/><line x1="150" y1="125" x2="382" y2="116" style="stroke:var(--f