('d0af69a0-f493-59fb-a3b6-a5eb02db7dc9', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '7ea4a576-84c8-4a0f-9474-20a442190683', 'a-level', '28.9', '9702 coursebook 28.9 · The nature of light: waves or particles?', 50, 50, 'A faint star gives an intensity of 1.0 × 10⁻¹¹ W m⁻² of light of wavelength 550 nm at the Earth. (a) Calculate the power entering a pupil of diameter 6.0 mm. (b) Calculate the number of photons entering per second. Take h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s and c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '781.8', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) P = 1.0 × 10⁻¹¹ × π × (3.0 × 10⁻³)² = 2.827 × 10⁻¹⁶ W. (b) n = 2.827 × 10⁻¹⁶ ÷ 3.616 × 10⁻¹⁹ = 782. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: pupil area. C1: power. M1: n = P/E. C1: value. A1: n = 782.', 5, NULL, NULL)
